                "reply_count": 9,
                "retweet_count": 4,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "If college athletes are forced to travel more than 2 time zones for a regular season game, they should receive a $250 to $1000 per game STIPEND to account for academic and mental health burden. \n\nThis amendment to SCORE would help put common sense back in athletics scheduling by disincentivizing absurd scheduling and fairly supplementing student athletes in Conferences and programs run by morons.\n\nRegular session competitions should be REGIONAL with minimal academic disruption and maximum local fan rivalry interest.\n\nFor example, if you are a Commissioner, Regent, University President or AD who thinks the west coast University of Washington volleyball team should be playing weeknight league games in east coast New Jersey, you are an idiot who has lost all sense of academic purpose and student athlete welfare in your greedy quest for football TV revenue. \ud83c\uddfa\ud83c\uddf8",
